#: ../../contributors_manual/krita_manual_readme.rst:26
msgid "Krita Manual Contribution Guide"
msgstr "Priročnik za prispevke za vodnik po Kriti"

#: ../../contributors_manual/krita_manual_readme.rst:28
#, fuzzy
msgid "Welcome to the Krita Manual Contribution Guide!"
msgstr "Dobrodošli v Priročniku za prispevke Krita!"

#: ../../contributors_manual/krita_manual_readme.rst:30
msgid ""
"If you're interested in contributing to Krita's documentation, you're in the "
"right place."
msgstr ""
"Če vas zanima prispevati k dokumentaciji za Krito, ste na pravem mestu."

#: ../../contributors_manual/krita_manual_readme.rst:32
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"Krita is (free) open source software, which effectively makes us a community "
"project with dozens of volunteers pitching in to make it better. This, of "
"course, requires we keep track of manuals and how-to's for new volunteers to "
"come in and help us. The various places we’ve done this have been rather "
"spread out, so the contributors' manual is an attempt to consolidate all the "
"information. It is therefore very technical in places."
msgstr ""
"Krita je (brezplačna) odprtokodna programska oprema, ki nas učinkovito "
"naredi skupnostni projekt z več deset prostovoljci, ki se vnašajo, da bo "
"bolje. To seveda zahteva, da spremljamo priročnike in navodila, da pridejo "
"novi prostovoljci in nam pomagajo. Različni kraji, ki smo jih naredili, so "
"bili precej razprodani, zato je priročnik za prispevke poskus konsolidirati "
"vse informacije. Zato je zelo tehnična na mestih."

#: ../../contributors_manual/krita_manual_readme.rst:34
msgid "This documentation will include:"
msgstr "Ta dokumentacija bo vključevala:"

#: ../../contributors_manual/krita_manual_readme.rst:36
msgid "A reference manual for Krita"
msgstr "Referenčni priročnik za Krito"

#: ../../contributors_manual/krita_manual_readme.rst:37
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"This one is probably what everyone is expecting when they look up Krita's "
"documentation. Dry, basic, 'what does this button do' type of information."
msgstr ""
"Ta je verjetno tisto, kar vsi pričakujejo, ko poiščijo Kritino "
"dokumentacijo. Suhe, osnovne, \"kaj ta gumb počne\" vrsta informacij."

#: ../../contributors_manual/krita_manual_readme.rst:39
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"We've found over the past two years that for certain types of users, a "
"reference manual, even with some examples, just isn't enough. The manual "
"should also provide fast and concise explanations for things, and provide a "
"basic workflow for preparing an image for the web."
msgstr ""
"V zadnjih dveh letih smo ugotovili, da za določene vrste uporabnikov "
"referenčni priročnik, tudi z nekaterimi primeri, le ni dovolj. Priročnik bi "
"moral zagotoviti tudi hitra in jedrnata pojasnila za stvari in zagotoviti "
"osnovni potek dela za pripravo slike za splet."

#: ../../contributors_manual/krita_manual_readme.rst:41
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"We also have found that certain concepts, such as color management and layer "
"handling are far more advanced in Krita than the average artist is used to. "
"Krita is free and many of its users will not have formal training in digital "
"artwork. So there is no pre-existing artist-focused knowledge on how to use "
"color management or filter layers."
msgstr ""
"Ugotovili smo tudi, da so določeni koncepti, kot sta upravljanje barv in "
"ravnanje s plastmi, v Kriti veliko naprednejši, kot je navajenega "
"povprečnega umetnika. Krita je brezplačna in številni njeni uporabniki ne "
"bodo imeli formalnega usposabljanja na področju digitalnih umetniških del. "
"Torej ni že obstoječega znanja, osredotočenega na umetnika, kako uporabljati "
"upravljanje barv ali filtre plasti."

#: ../../contributors_manual/krita_manual_readme.rst:42
#, fuzzy
#| msgid "General settings"
msgid "General concept tutorials."
msgstr "Splošne nastavitve"

#: ../../contributors_manual/krita_manual_readme.rst:43
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"In addition there are systems that are unique to Krita, for example the "
"brush system, the transform masks, the alpha inheritance and the perspective "
"assistants. Finally, there are users who aren't familiar with even standard "
"painting workflows, and are not flexible enough to understand how to port a "
"tutorial for SAI or Photoshop to Krita."
msgstr ""
"Poleg tega obstajajo sistemi, ki so edinstveni za Krita, na primer ščetka "
"sistem, transform maske, alfa dedovanje in perspektive pomočnikov. Končno, "
"obstajajo uporabniki, ki niso seznanjeni s celo standardnih slikarskih "
"delovnih tokov, in niso dovolj prilagodljivi, da bi razumeli, kako port "
"tutorial za SAI ali Photoshop krita."

#: ../../contributors_manual/krita_manual_readme.rst:44
#, fuzzy
msgid "A list of known tutorials and video tutorials"
msgstr "Seznam znanih vaj in video tutorials"

#: ../../contributors_manual/krita_manual_readme.rst:45
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"Apparently, one of the great things about Krita's team is how we connect "
"with artists and acknowledge that they're doing cool stuff. The same should "
"count for tutorials, especially because there are ways of using Krita and "
"ways of approaching painting that are unique and we should encourage people "
"to share their knowledge."
msgstr ""
"Očitno je ena od odličnih stvari pri Kritini ekipi, kako se povežemo z "
"umetniki in priznamo, da počnejo kul stvari. Enako bi moralo šteti za vaje, "
"še posebej zato, ker obstajajo načini uporabe Krita in načini približevanja "
"slikanje, ki so edinstveni in moramo spodbujati ljudi, da delijo svoje "
"znanje."

#: ../../contributors_manual/krita_manual_readme.rst:46
msgid "Contributors' Manual"
msgstr "Priročnik za avtorje prispevkov"

#: ../../contributors_manual/krita_manual_readme.rst:47
msgid "What you're reading right now!"
msgstr "Kar zdaj berete!"

#: ../../contributors_manual/krita_manual_readme.rst:48
msgid "krita.org tutorials"
msgstr "Vaje krita.org"

#: ../../contributors_manual/krita_manual_readme.rst:49
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"There have been a bunch of tutorials on the krita.org and the krita-"
"foundation.tumblr.com, the former focusing on explaining how to use a new "
"feature and the later stimulated by user request."
msgstr ""
"Obstajal je kup vaj na krita.org in krita-foundation.tumblr.com, prej se "
"osredotoča na razlago, kako uporabljati novo funkcijo in kasneje spodbudila "
"z zahtevo uporabnika."

#: ../../contributors_manual/krita_manual_readme.rst:51
msgid "FAQ"
msgstr "Pogosto zastavljena vprašanja"

#: ../../contributors_manual/krita_manual_readme.rst:51
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"This one is already online and a merger of the different FAQs that we had. "
"It's currently being translated and we hope to keep this one the primary one "
"to update."
msgstr ""
"Ta je že na spletu in združitev različnih pogostih vprašanj, ki smo jih "
"imeli. Trenutno se prevaja in upamo, da bo ta primarna za posodobitev."

#: ../../contributors_manual/krita_manual_readme.rst:54
msgid "For first timers"
msgstr "Za začetnike"

#: ../../contributors_manual/krita_manual_readme.rst:56
#, fuzzy
msgid "Unlike Mediawiki, Sphinx works more like how we write code for Krita."
msgstr ""
"Za razliko od Mediawikija, Sfinga deluje bolj kot kako pišemo kodo za Krito."

#: ../../contributors_manual/krita_manual_readme.rst:58
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"First things first, you will want to talk to us! For this you can join us in "
"the chatroom \"#krita\" via matrix. A introduction about Matrix is given "
"`here <https://community.kde.org/Matrix>`_. Create a matrix on webchat.kde."
"org account and join the #krita:kde.org channel. Or more importantly, make "
"an account at `identity.kde.org <https://identity.kde.org/>`_. The account "
"you make at identity can be used to both access invent.kde.org as well as "
"the `phabricator`_, where we organise Krita development."
msgstr ""
"Najprej se boš hotel pogovoriti z nami! Za to se nam lahko pridružite v "
"chatroomu \"#krita\" preko matrice. Uvod o Matrici je podan \"tukaj <https://"
"community.kde.org/Matrix>\"_. Ustvarite matriko v webchat.kde.org in se "
"pridružite kanalu #krita:kde.org. Ali še pomembneje, naredite račun na "
"\"identity.kde.org <https://identity.kde.org/>\"_. Račun, ki ga naredite po "
"identiteti, se lahko uporablja tako za dostop invent.kde.org kot tudi za "
"\"phabricator\"_, kjer organiziramo krita razvoj."

#: ../../contributors_manual/krita_manual_readme.rst:60
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"Sphinx works by writing simple text files with reStructuredText mark up, and "
"then it takes those text files and turns them into the manual. We keep track "
"of changes in the manual by putting them into a version control system "
"called :program:`Git`."
msgstr ""
"Sfinga deluje tako, da napiše preproste besedilne datoteke z oznako "
"prestrukturiranjaText, nato pa vzame te besedilne datoteke in jih spremeni v "
"priročnik. Sledimo spremembam v priročniku tako, da jih damo v sistem za "
"nadzor različice, imenovan :p rogram:'Git'."

#: ../../contributors_manual/krita_manual_readme.rst:65
#, fuzzy
#| msgctxt "Context: dynamic sensors"
#| msgid "Drawing angle"
msgid "Making changes"
msgstr "Kot risanja"

#: ../../contributors_manual/krita_manual_readme.rst:67
#, fuzzy
msgid ""
"Because we use Git, there's only a few people who can put things into the "
"version control system, so if you want to make changes you will need to put "
"it up for review."
msgstr ""
"Ker uporabljamo Git, obstaja le nekaj ljudi, ki lahko stvari dajo v sistem "
"za nadzor različic, tako da če želite narediti spremembe, boste morali dati "
"gor za pregled."

#: ../../contributors_manual/krita_manual_readme.rst:73
